# __PACK_NAME__

A `@moba2d/core` content pack, scaffolded by `moba2d-pack-new`: one
champion (__CHAMPION__), one map, one ability — enough to typecheck, load
into core, and start growing from.

## Run this next

```
npm install
npm test
npm run check-seams
```

Both `test` and `check-seams` have to stay green — they are this pack's
own gate, not core's, and `npm install` never runs them for you.

## Where things live

- `pack.ts` — the whole pack's declaration: the roster, the map, and the
  code half core's registry calls to build real spell classes.
- `spells/` — one file per ability. `__CHAMPION___Q.ts` is the example;
  read it before writing a second one — the shape (tuning as exported
  constants, a memoized factory, a separate spell-object class) is not
  decoration, it is what keeps two different callers from building two
  different, `instanceof`-incompatible classes with the same name.
- `tests/` — one test per ability, driven through `pressSpell`, never
  through a lifecycle hook like `onSpellCast()` directly: a hook-calling
  test cannot see activation, cooldown, resource cost or targeting
  rejection, and stays green against an ability that does not work at all.
- `map.ts` / `geometry.ts` — the world this pack ships. `geometry.ts` is
  fetched lazily, so a pregame picker never downloads the walls and lanes
  just to list this map's name.

## Add another ability

```
moba2d-pack-add spell <Name> --champion __CHAMPION__ --slot W
```

writes the spell file and its test, and registers both in `pack.ts`.

